  "review_notes": [
    "All 13 functions are immediate file children, each explicitly terminated by end. No nested definitions, classes, methods, duplicate names or inheritance occur. Primary function loadjson agrees with loadjson.m.",
    "All accepted targets are unique exact-case file-local functions. Inputs, outputs and assignment roots in each caller do not bind any of these target names; no imports or nested lexical ancestors occur.",
    "parse_array: eval(arraystr) at L261 vetoes the entire callable scope, including sites before eval and unreachable paths; catch does not restore binding confidence. The handle @unescapejsonstring at L263 is separately excluded.",
    "parseStr: bare keyboard; at L390 is an unknown-workspace command invocation, even in a supposedly unreachable otherwise branch. It vetoes all five same-file call sites in that callable. The declaration and incoming calls remain valid.",
    "No eligible same-file sites occur in error_pos, skip_whitespace, unescapejsonstring or sscanf_prep. parse2darray calls external match_bracket at L536 (excluded) and local sscanf_prep at L537 (included).",
    "Parenthesis expressions on bound inputstr, data, objid, esc, str, object, poShow, arraystr, astr, dims and other assigned roots are indexing, never calls. Field/indexed assignments do not create callable targets.",
    "External helpers include varargin2struct, jsonopt, jdatadecode, fast_match_bracket, nestbracket2dim, encodevarname and match_bracket. None has a declaration in this file, so none is in the call denominator.",
    "containers.Map at L455 is dotted constructor syntax; anonymous-function bodies at L285 and L509 and replacement-expression string at L520 are excluded. Bare values such as pwd, inf and nargin in expressions are not direct parenthesized call sites or standalone command statements.",
    "L103 error_pos has fewer arguments than its signature; static eligible call identity does not assert runtime validity. Corpus source is not repaired or executed.",
    "This corpus is intentionally limited: synthetic fixtures, not this manifest, cover classes, namespaces, nested scopes and duplicate names."
  ]
